    "problem": "Calculate the product ${I}_{2}B$ given that ${I}_{2}$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$",
    "worked_solution": "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n{I}_{2}\\cdot B=B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
